# python -- needed by glibc's own configure, which refuses to run without it:
#   "These critical programs are missing or too old: bison python"
#
# It was a chapter-7 temporary tool in duct/chroot and never a package, which
# meant duct/builder could not rebuild glibc at all.
SRC_URL=$PYTHON_URL
SRC_SHA256=$PYTHON_SHA256
SRC_DIR=$PYTHON_SRCDIR

# --without-ensurepip because pip would reach the network during the build, and
# nothing in Duct needs it yet. --enable-shared so anything embedding Python
# links against libpython rather than statically absorbing it.
# ssl is built again. It could not be under OpenSSL 4.0, which made the ASN1_*
# string types opaque while Python 3.13's _ssl still reaches into them; the
# distribution is on 3.5 LTS now and the module compiles. Kept in the history
# rather than erased, because "why does this interpreter have no ssl" is a
# question worth being able to answer.
#
# There is deliberately no py_cv_module__ssl here now. The module is wanted, and
# install.sh asserts it was actually produced rather than trusting the probe.
CONFIGURE_ARGS="--enable-shared --without-ensurepip --without-static-libpython --enable-optimizations=no"
